@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Identity & Access Context" as IAC {
  [Login Screen (Vaadin)] as LoginUI
}

package "Registrar Workspace (application shell)" as Workspace {
  [Dashboard] as DashboardUI
}

package "Course Catalog Context" as CCC {
  [Course Catalog UI (Vaadin)] as CourseUI
}

package "Students Context (future)" as StudentsCtx #line.dashed {
  [Students UI] as StudentsUI #line.dashed
}

package "Scheduling & Enrollment Context (future)" as SchedCtx #line.dashed {
  [Scheduling UI] as SchedUI #line.dashed
}

LoginUI --> DashboardUI : grants an authenticated session
DashboardUI --> CourseUI : Course Catalog tile
DashboardUI ..> StudentsUI : Students tile (not built yet)
DashboardUI ..> SchedUI : Scheduling tile (not built yet)

note bottom of Workspace
  Not a bounded context of its own — no new aggregate,
  no persistent state (see README: "why no new
  aggregate"). Just the application-layer landing page
  that composes navigation into whichever contexts
  exist, so no single context has to own "".
end note

note bottom of StudentsCtx
  Module 4's ERD already scoped these two groups
  of tables (People; Scheduling & enrollment) —
  this is why the Dashboard has room for them now,
  without redesigning it when they arrive.
end note

@enduml
